def PR(n,title,cnums,as_he,plausible,art,why,worth,refs):
 cc=[c for c in claims if int(c['id'].split('C')[1]) in cnums]
 problems.append({'id':f'MP-SA08-{n}','title':title,'occurrences':[{'claim':c['id'],'cote':c['cote'],'scans':c['scans'],'lines':c['lines'],'his_words':c['his_statement']} for c in cc],'as_he_states':as_he,'plausible_today':plausible,'state_of_art':art,'why_open':why,'worth':worth,'refs':refs})
PR(30,'Universally flasque divided powers',[103,104],'Positive divided powers should preserve the required universal flasqueness; the attempted flat-to-contractible proof is retracted.','Prove preservation for explicitly simplicially contractible models, or impose the exact projectivity/splitting needed for the intended sheaf notion.','The particular Φ model is handled on227 and Cartan§7; arbitrary flat acyclicity is insufficient.','The page itself records a failed inference; no historical account of abandonment is supplied.','Worth a short reconstruction run because it isolates the actual missing hypothesis instead of creating a broad new conjecture.',[CA,DK])
PR(31,'Primed localization automorphism groups',[107,108],'Determine the two groups obtained after allowing completed differential PD morphisms without grading.','Fix the coefficient completion and morphism category, then compute its isotropy rather than infer triviality from connectedness.','No exact published classification was located in the recorded searches; Cartan’s cohomological comparison is not such a classification.','The text changes categories and contains an ambiguous ponctuels/pointés reading; no causal explanation beyond the unfinished calculation is given.','High-value archival direction, but first requires a precise category and an ink check at104/108.',[CA,ST])
PR(32,'Uniform weight threshold',[111],'Suspect that λ_n(p) can be independent of simplex dimension n.','For the standard PD simplex forms, weight r≥p gives the degree-p comparison uniformly in n.','Established for the displayed model by231–233 and Cartan§7; not an all-theories uniformity theorem.','The manuscript marks the earlier bound tentative; later calculations supply the model-specific answer.','Worth a few hours only to document the exact transition from the tentative bound to the inclusive final range.',[CA])
PR(33,'Converse quasi-flasqueness',[112,113],'The stated quasi-flasque growth condition is perhaps equivalent to the comparison property.','Formulate a precise necessary-and-sufficient condition in the chosen simplex-sheaf category before testing the converse.','Only sufficient comparison axioms were matched in Cartan; the unrestricted converse was not located.','The manuscript says sans doute rather than proving the converse.','Worth developing only after the definitions of τ∞ and quasi-flasque are fixed from all packets.',[CA])
PR(34,'Uniqueness groupoid',[114],'The groupoid completion of admissible generalized theories should be connected and simply connected.','A theorem about the localization groupoid with stated admissible arrows; contractibility of its entire nerve would be a distinct strengthening.','No exact theorem matched; Mandell’s E∞ theorem concerns spaces and a different functor.','The page gives a conjecture and possible proof mechanism, with no later resolution in the supplied sheets.','Potentially valuable, but a research run should first construct explicit common models in a small subcategory.',[CA,'Mandell2006'])
PR(35,'Common refinements and fractions',[115],'Admissible common refinements and precomposition equalizations may establish a fraction calculus.','Verify the precise Ore/equalization conditions for the stated category, separately from groupoid connectedness.','No matching theorem located in the bounded searches; generic model-category intuition is not an exact answer.','The writer leaves left/right fraction alternatives and question marks.','A concrete small-case obstruction or construction is a realistic first research task.',[CA])
PR(36,'Coefficient augmentation after duality',[118],'The dual quotient diagram suggests an augmentation onto the dual of Sbar.','Assume the inclusion Sbar→S splits, or specify a class of test coefficients for which Hom is exact.','The standard polynomial-coalgebra example is split; the arbitrary coefficient assertion is not established by ordinary duality.','An uncertain arrow and implicit exactness create the gap; the source gives no explanation of an abandoned generalization.','Useful as a focused correction of the generalized coefficient formalism.',[ST])
PR(37,'Structured coefficient colimits',[120],'Covariance in coefficient data and commutation with colimits are asserted.','Prove ordinary colimit preservation in X by the Kan-extension adjunction, then separately specify admissible colimits of coalgebra/PD coefficient data.','The X-variable part is formal; no exact unrestricted coefficient-category theorem was matched.','The manuscript moves from modules to structured data without recording all preservation assumptions.','Worth a short categorical audit, not an unbounded derived-descent project.',[DK,ST])
PR(38,'Dual Stokes compatibility',[124],'Construct the κ_n and verify dκ_n=∂κ_(n−1), with coherent signs.','Use the standard simplex orientation and corrected degree/sign conventions to build a chain map.','CartanTh2 gives integration under its axioms; the exact manuscript signs at137 remain a transcription task.','The source displays scratched signs and a partly cancelled dualization calculation.','High feasibility: one run can write a complete convention sheet and compare every face term.',[CA])
PR(39,'Integral simplex normalization',[127,128],'Determine the coefficients γ and complete the recurrence at141.','For all nonnegative indices, γ=1 under positive standard orientation and C_ab=binom(a+b,a).','Resolved by beta integration and the general generating-function calculation; finite exact certificates retained.','The only remaining issue is the placement of inserted factors and indices in the ink, not the value of the normalized integral.','Worth an editorial run to settle the crowded corrections; no new theorem is required.',['DLMF514'])
PR(40,'Tate full faithfulness in equal characteristic',[137,175,179],'Remove the characteristic-zero restriction in p-primary generic-fibre extension arguments.','For any DVR R of characteristic p and p-divisible groups G,H, restriction Hom_R→Hom_K is bijective.','deJong1998Cor1.2 proves it without a p-basis restriction; Th1.1 for F-crystals has that extra hypothesis; 1999erratum is accounted for.','deJong explicitly identifies this as the SGA IX problem.','No new research needed for the theorem; an annotation should point to the exact corollary and erratum.',['deJong1998','deJong1999Erratum',S])
PR(41,'Potentially semistable integral monodromy',[139,140],'Is e^(−1)v always integer-valued? The elliptic case is asserted.','State the normalized pairing on the exact potentially semistable character lattices, with descent and ramification conventions.','SGAIX9.7 still asks the question in1972;10.4 proves the semistable case. No exact general later settlement was verified by this run.','The donor supplies no reason beyond the remaining denominator issue; absence of a later hit does not establish present openness.','Worth a dedicated literature run with degeneration-data experts and explicit examples before proposing new mathematics.',[S,'Coleman2000'])
PR(42,'p-primary nondegeneracy in component duality',[141,142],'Complete the argument that monodromy gives perfect duality, including ℓ=p.','Use the semistable integrality/nondegeneracy theorem10.4 and the exact lattice-cokernel statement11.5.','PublishedSGAIX proves this semistable assertion; general non-semistable component pairings are a separate problem.','The local leaf invokes a deeper theorem elsewhere, rather than leaving a freestanding conjecture.','Editorially useful; no independent new proof is needed in this dossier.',[S])
PR(43,'Correct interval extension theorem',[145,146,147],'Repair the retracted universal extension theorem using2B_i=0.','Prove necessity and sufficiency under the exact endpoint, PD, differential, naturality, coefficient and completion conditions.','The necessary obstruction and cancellation are clear; the unrestricted version has an explicit counterexample. No exact later classification was located.','The page itself says faux tel quel and requests correcting the corollaries.','A strong research direction: one run can formalize the relations and prove the corrected finite-dimensional extension lemma.',[ST])
PR(44,'Semidirect decomposition of natural maps',[149,150,151,152],'The questioned G,H,Ω diagram suggests a semidirect description.','Work first with polynomial versus completed coefficients separately and restrict to units if a group is intended.','Substitution law and torsion intersection are settled algebra; a full semidirect theorem was not matched.','The text corrects group to monoid, and nontrivial G∩H in torsion makes a naive decomposition fail.','Worth developing after43; a prime-two example is a practical initial test.',[ST])
PR(45,'Free alternating PD proof',[153],'The free theorem is stated and its proof left blank.','Prove the universal property by adjoining even divided-power and odd exterior generators over the given PD base.','Standard gradedPD algebra, available in Roby/Cartan and Stacks09PF.','No historical reason for omitting the proof is given; its formal nature is not evidence of an open theorem.','A short explanatory proof is useful, but this is low novelty.',[ST,'Roby1963'])
PR(46,'Inhomogeneous PD identities',[154],'Verify the remaining PD axioms after extending γ to x+u, including iteration.','Keep the strict odd-product-zero compatibility for sums and spell out exactly where the ordinary PD axiom is intended.','Modern gradedPD conventions match the homogeneous part; the broader inhomogeneous extension is a convention-dependent elementary calculation.','The writer checks several identities and stops before iteration.','Worth a bounded algebra audit, especially at2, before using ungraded morphisms.',[ST])
PR(47,'Characteristic-p Cartier operations',[159],'Describe the characteristic-p homology and operations for ordinaryDR andPDKoszul.','For finite free modules, use the polynomial Cartier isomorphism and degreewise duality; distinguish arbitrary flat modules and unspecified extra operations.','Classical Cartier gives the polynomialDR cohomology; the manuscript’s full operation request is not precise enough to identify a single later theorem.','The pages name Cartier but leave the construction unfinished.','Moderate interest: a first run can give coordinate formulas and their Frobenius-twisted functoriality.',['Cartier1957',BM])
PR(48,'Normalization compatibility',[165],'Check differential/naturality compatibility of the representability formula on225.','Fix variance and the exact exterior contraction, including the i=0 case, then compare to the Dold–Kan disk representable.','Standard Dold–Puppe machinery supplies the result; the cancelled226 formula is not used.','The writer says the compatibility remains to check.','Highly feasible editorial task, with signs as the main source of error.',[DK])
PR(49,'Derived exterior powers convention',[167],'Is the general formula for a projective complex true, sauf erreur?','Use Dold–Puppe derived exterior powers and décalage, not naive termwise exterior powers of a chain complex.','BMT2016Prop3.5 records integral décalage for finiteprojective modules, citingBousfield,Quillen,Illusie; k[1] is a valid special case.','The same exterior symbol can denote inequivalent constructions in small characteristic.','Worth a short notation comparison; do not advertise the naive false formulation as open.',[BM,DK])
PR(50,'Minimal normalized exterior model',[168],'NΛ^iΨ=k[i] is probable.','The exact equality holds up to the canonical normalized-model identification over every base ring.','Resolved by integral Dold–Kan splitting and binomial-rank inversion; direct certificates retained.','The manuscript first hedges, then uses the assertion on231.','One editorial proof paragraph suffices; no new research needed.',[DK,BM])
PR(51,'Symmetric and divided-power NB',[169],'The NB suggests additional K(k,i) variants but has unclear duality/variance.','First settle the symbols and variance on the scan; the natural simplicialΓ²/Sym² interpretation is false overZ.','Explicit normalized differentials−2 and−1 give conditional counterexamples; BMT2016describes genuinely derivedΓfunctors.','The transcription does not identify a unique theorem; its mathematical ambiguity blocks a fate assignment.','High priority for scan review, low value for conjecture-building until the text is fixed.',[BM])
PR(52,'Completed coefficient theory',[174],'The filtration S^[i] starts a new completion argument.','Read the continuation235–281 before stating a completeness, exactness or limit-commutation theorem.','Currentpacket gives setup only; other-agent continuation supplies the claim.','The physical packet boundary cuts off the discussion.','Worth integration across packets; no conjecture should be invented from the heading.',[CA])
PR(53,'BT specialization rigidity proof',[178],'The proof of5.2.5 is called easy and left to the reader.','Prove zero/isogeny/isomorphism detection for pro-ℓBTgroups over connectedNoetherianbase with the actual fibre and compatible system.','PublishedSGAIX5.2.5 retains the omitted proof and7.4.7proves the needed special cases.','The source gives no explanation beyond treating it as elementary.','An optional explanatory proof is useful, but it is not a modern open question.',[S])
PR(54,'All-primes orthogonality',[177],'Complete the p-primary orthogonality case.','Follow the biextension argument inSGAIX7.4.6–.7 rather than extrapolate prime-to-p etale duality.','The published source supplies the promised argument; deJonglaterupdates a separate Tate ingredient.','The leaf is a partial reduction with explicit forward references.','A source annotation is sufficient; avoid duplicating a large established proof.',[S,'deJong1998'])
PR(55,'Perfect duality of abelian parts',[176],'Show the isogeny of abelian parts is a perfect duality in full generality.','Use the canonical biextension and the stated connected trait assumptions.','SGAIX5.4 and7.4.6are exact publication matches.','The proof is deferred within the same work.','Low research novelty, high editorial value as a resolved forward reference.',[S])
PR(56,'Good reduction and completeness provisos',[179,180],'An older good-reduction conjecture is now announced; completeness is to be removed later.','Separate the established criterion5.10, the formal-construction completeness removal6.1, and equal-characteristic full faithfulness.','SGAIX publishes the first two; deJong1998§2supplies the equal-characteristic p-divisible good-reduction application.','These are distinct deferred steps, not one enduring conjecture.','Worth a chronology annotation with exact hypotheses and no new proof development.',[S,'deJong1998','deJong1999Erratum'])
PR(57,'Algebraic description of the uniformization lattice',[183],'The writer knows no purely algebraic-geometric description of i, and promises an arithmetic characterization.','Ask for a canonical construction from precise degeneration/1-motive data, indicating which formal or analytic ingredients are allowed.','SGAIX14.1.12a,p509 retains the statement; later algebraic degeneration frameworks are relevant but not automatically an exact solution.','The source calls i a more hidden structural element; it does not document a later abandonment.','Substantive direction after a dedicated source comparison; first specify the allowed category and input data.',[S,'Coleman2000'])
PR(58,'Dual uniformization sign',[184],'The dual lattice map may be its opposite.','Fix Poincare biextension and duality conventions, then compare the two embeddings with a Tate-curve test.','The question survives in the published original14.1.12b,p509; a paired-monodromy comparison does not automatically settle every sign.','This is an explicit convention doubt, not evidence of a false uniformization theorem.','Excellent bounded task: a complete convention table and one rank-one example should decide the mathematical sign.',[S,'Coleman2000'])
PR(59,'Algebraic and analytic Tate compatibility',[186],'The exact sequence from rigid uniformization should match the algebraic Tate sequence.','Compare maps, twists and sign conventions under the precise semistable reduction assumptions.','SGAIX14.2continues the argument; Coleman§2addresses equality of the associated monodromy pairings.','The supplied leaf cuts the proof before its end.','Worth tracing the continuation and source conventions, rather than treating it as a new conjecture.',[S,'Coleman2000'])
